cff-version: 1.2.0

title: "KELLY CODE: The Theory of Identity Survival"

message: >
  If you use this work in academic research,
  please cite it using the metadata provided in this file.

type: article

authors:
  - family-names: "Van-Orton"
    given-names: "Nicholas"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4628-1871"

abstract: >
  KELLY CODE is a multidisciplinary research project investigating
  how identities survive changes in environments, roles, systems,
  and historical contexts. The work integrates visual culture,
  art history, cultural studies, philosophy, and identity theory
  into a unified framework describing long-term identity continuity.

